 "title": "Scotland County, Missouri",
 "text": "Scotland County, Missouri\nSelect “Accept all” to agree to our use of cookies and similar technologies to enhance your browsing experience, security, analytics and customization. Select ”Manage cookies” to make more choices or opt out.\nManage cookies Accept all\nSkip to main content\nAbout\nCounty Use Tax\nPress Releases\nElected Officials\nElection Results\nContact\nAbout County Use Tax Press Releases Elected Officials Election Results Contact\nWelcome to Scotland County, Missouri\nWorld War Two Memorial on Courthouse Lawn\nScotland County Missouri has many amenities and services to offer our citizens and visitors. If you’re considering moving a business to Scotland County, we have a hospital, accredited schools, an airport, and a local radio station.\nMany people enjoy our outdoor recreational areas in addition to our quiet rural setting. Public recreational areas include Lake Show Me , Ella Ewing Lake , and the Indian Hills Conservation Area .\nOur rich history has left us with numerous historic landmarks including our Scotland County Courthouse, the Downing House Museum, the Boyer House and Museum, the Memphis Depot Museum, Pheasant Airplane, and the Barnett Statue.\nFor Civil War history buffs, Scotland County was the location of The Battle of Vasser Hill.\nWe invite you to visit us here in Scotland County and to make this a regular place to visit or better yet, to join us by relocating here.\nLocal Resources\nScotland County Hospital\nScotland County R-1 School District\nScotland County Fair\nScotland County MU Extension\nMODot Scotland County Information\nScotland County Health Department\nScotland County Memorial Library\nMemphis Area Chamber of Commerce\nDowning House Museum\nScotland County Road Map (PDF)\nHome Scotland County Road Map (PDF) Accessibility Terms of Use Search Contact\nWebsite 54 Design Group",
